# MT (MEMORY CHANNEL WRITE/TAG) — Set-direction wire frames, hand-derived
#
# Manual: "FT-991A HF/VHF/UHF ALL MODE TRANSCEIVER — CAT Operation Reference Manual",
#   YAESU MUSEN CO., LTD., Copyright 2017.
# Printed revision: "1711-D" (printed bottom-right of the back cover, PDF page 20).
#   No revision string is printed on the title page.
# Chart used: the MT command detail block, printed folio 12 = PDF page 13.
#   Layout counted from the SET chart (the Set chart is the one the brief asks for and is
#   the only MT chart that carries the Set-direction reading of P7). The ANSWER chart on the
#   same block was counted independently and is byte-for-byte the same 41-position layout;
#   the READ chart is a separate 6-position layout, recorded as a comment below.
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026.
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTH (Set): 41 bytes, terminator included.
#   Count A (left-to-right through the printed position numbers): row 1 = 1..10 all filled,
#   row 2 = 11..20 all filled, row 3 = 21..30 all filled, row 4 = 31..40 all filled,
#   row 5 = 41..50 with only cell 41 filled (";"). Last filled position = 41.
#   Count B (row totals): 5 printed rows x 10 numbered cells = 50 numbered positions;
#   filled cells 10+10+10+10+1 = 41. Both counts agree; no third look was needed.
#   Charts were re-rendered at 600 dpi (position numbers unambiguous at that magnification);
#   the legend that interleaves with the chart rows was cropped separately at 600 dpi, and
#   the clarifier-direction glyph at 1800 dpi.
#
# POSITION-BY-POSITION FIELD MAP (Set chart, MT block, printed folio 12)
#   pos 1      "M"                     command letter (printed literally in the chart)
#   pos 2      "T"                     command letter (printed literally in the chart)
#   pos 3-5    P1  (3 positions)       legend: "P0/1  001-117 (Memory Channel)"
#   pos 6-14   P2  (9 positions)       legend: "P2    VFO-A Frequency (Hz)"
#   pos 15-19  P3  (5 positions)       legend: "P3  Clarifier Direction +: Plus Shift, --: Minus Shift"
#                                              "Clarifier Offset: 0000 - 9999 (Hz)"
#   pos 20     P4  (1 position)        legend: "P4  0: RX CLAR "OFF"    1: RX CLAR "ON""
#   pos 21     P5  (1 position)        legend: "P5  0: TX CLAR "OFF"    1: TX CLAR "ON""
#   pos 22     P6  (1 position)        legend: "P6  MODE  1: LSB   2: USB   3: CW   4: FM   5: AM   6: RTTY-LSB   7: CW-R"
#                                              "8: DATA-LSB   9: RTTY-USB   A: DATA-FM   B: FM-N   C: DATA-USB"
#                                              "D: AM-N   E: C4FM"
#   pos 23     P7  (1 position)        legend: "P7  Set: 0: (Fixed) / Read: 0: VFO  1: Memory"
#   pos 24     P8  (1 position)        legend: "P8  0: CTCSS "OFF"   1: CTCSS ENC/DEC   2: CTCSS ENC   3: DCS ENC/DEC"
#                                              "4: DCS ENC"
#   pos 25-26  P9  (2 positions)       legend: "P9  00: (Fixed)"
#   pos 27     P10 (1 position)        legend: "P10 0: Simplex    1: Plus Shift    2: Minus Shift"
#   pos 28     P11 (1 position)        legend: "P11 0: (Fixed)"
#   pos 29-40  P12 (12 positions)      legend: "P12 TAG Characters (up to 12 characters) (ASCII)"
#   pos 41     ";"                     terminator (printed literally in the chart)
#
# TAG ON/OFF FLAG: the MT chart prints NO tag ON/OFF flag position. The position that sits
#   immediately before the tag field, P11 (position 28), is printed "0: (Fixed)". The fixed
#   value is therefore "0" and every vector below carries "0" there. No flag was invented,
#   and no "TAG OFF" vector exists in this file because the chart offers no such position.
#
# BYTES THE MANUAL DETERMINES vs INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   Manual-determined: the command letters "MT"; the field widths (counted); the terminator
#   ";"; the P1 range 001-117; the P2 unit (Hz) and its 9-digit width; the P3 offset range
#   0000-9999; every P4/P5/P6/P8/P10 index and label; P7 = "0" (Set direction, printed
#   "Set: 0: (Fixed)"); P9 = "00" (printed "(Fixed)"); P11 = "0" (printed "(Fixed)").
#   INHERITED-ASSUMED (1) — TAG PADDING: the manual says only "up to 12 characters" and
#     never states what a shorter tag is padded with, nor whether the tag is left- or
#     right-justified in the 12 positions. Every vector below left-justifies the tag and
#     pads the remaining positions with ASCII SPACE (0x20). SPACE was chosen because the
#     manual's own general note (printed folio 2, PDF page 3) says unusable parameter digits
#     "should be filled using any character except the ASCII control codes (00 to 1Fh) and
#     the terminator (;)", and 0x20 is neither. This is an assumption, not a reading.
#   INHERITED-ASSUMED (2) — MINUS CLARIFIER DIRECTION BYTE: the P3 legend prints
#     "+: Plus Shift, --: Minus Shift" — two hyphen glyphs, verified at 1800 dpi with a
#     clear gap between them — yet the chart gives P3 exactly 5 positions and the offset is
#     4 digits, leaving exactly ONE position for the direction. Vectors below use a single
#     "-" (0x2D) for the minus direction. Recorded, not resolved.
#   INHERITED-ASSUMED (3) — TAG CHARACTER SET: the legend says "(ASCII)" but prints no
#     permitted-character list. Tags below are upper-case A-Z and digits 0-9 only, invented
#     strings, no real call signs.
#
# MT READ REQUEST FRAME, exactly as the block's Read chart prints it
#   Read chart positions: 1 "M", 2 "T", 3 P0, 4 P0, 5 P0, 6 ";" — counted length 6 bytes.
#   For memory channel 001 the Read request is:      MT001;
#
# COMMAND-LIST vs DETAIL-BLOCK, MT directions — BOTH readings recorded verbatim, unresolved
#   Command list, printed folio 3 (PDF page 4), row verbatim:
#     "MT | MEMORY CHANNEL WRITE/TAG | Set: O | Read: O | Ans.: O | AI: X"
#   Detail block, printed folio 12 (PDF page 13), verbatim as charts:
#     Set    row: chart printed and filled ("M T P1 P1 P1 P2 ... P12 ;", 41 positions)
#     Read   row: chart printed and filled ("M T P0 P0 P0 ;", 6 positions)
#     Answer row: chart printed and filled ("M T P1 P1 P1 P2 ... P12 ;", 41 positions)
#   The two readings AGREE that MT supports Set, Read and Answer. Recorded, not resolved.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED. No frame below has been sent to or read from a radio.
#
mt_ch001_7m100_lsb_tag_full_12char	MT001007100000+0000001000000HIGHLANDNET1;
mt_ch002_14m250_usb_tag_short_padded	MT002014250000+0000002000000CLUB        ;
